  "slug": "current-cosmological-53cb",
  "summary": "Four November 2026 preprints apply DESI, HSC-SSP and JWST data to protoclusters, cluster lenses, group baryons and Little Red Dot demographics.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is survey-based mapping of structure and its tracers across cosmic time, not a dark-energy test. DESI DR1 physical quasar pairs at z≈2, with separations up to 2.5 Mpc, trace protocluster environments consistent with ΛCDM mock predictions. VENUS supplies strong-lensing models for 57 JWST clusters with 1733 multiply-imaged systems and derives mass scaling relations. Localized FRBs crossmatched with DESI galaxy groups give a tentative 143 pc cm^-3 excess dispersion measure for group-intersecting sight lines, a low-significance baryon probe. An HSC-SSP spectroscopic search finds the Little Red Dot number density falling ~35x from z~4-8 to z~2.1-2.6 while the luminosity-function knee does not evolve. The items differ in tracer and scale; the shared element is large-area survey data.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
